From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yewsifofficial <yewsifofficial@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:32:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] nextendo: stamp every line with the time, and read the login
 this game sends

The working emulator's trace and ours now agree on everything that can be
counted. Its NAT check and ours are the same twenty datagrams and ten
replies, split the same way between the two responders. Its sockets are
parked and adopted in the same order as ours, it reports the same errno
value for a read with nothing to read, and it is handed the same peer we
are. The one thing left to compare is when each step happened: after its
three datagrams to the sinkhole it polls an empty socket for another 0.96
seconds and only then reaches the peer, while this engine gives up somewhere
in that second. That emulator's log is stamped to the millisecond and ours
carried no time at all, so the comparison could not be made.

So every Nextendo line now opens with the milliseconds since the first one.
The clock is monotonic and the start is the first line of the run, which is
what makes two traces of the same minute lie flat against each other.

The login decoder also covered the wrong methods. This game logs in with
ticket granting method 6, LoginWithContext, and only 1, 2 and 3 were read,
so the one message that says who the server thinks we are went past
unexamined. Method 6 wraps the username in a structure rather than opening
with it, so the PID is now looked for as the digits it is written as,
anywhere in the body, which holds for either shape. Checked against vectors
built the way the server builds them, in both shapes, with and without the
nnex claim and with a PID that is not ours.

Upstream-Status: fork-only (online play is out of nxnative's scope)
Reason: Nextendo online play for Super Smash Bros. Ultimate
Issue: yewsiff/NX2Apple (no tracker: issues are disabled on this fork)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017xdHQoEipBX2wTqN8BNnMv
